{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2530,2595p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '2700,2897p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '3030,3378p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"\n\n(def ^:private kernel-unexercised-reasons\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_unexercised.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-exercise-entries\n  [inventory fixtures results]\n  (vec\n    (for [{:keys [symbol arities disposition]} inventory\n          :when (= :admitted disposition)\n          n arities\n          :let [direct (vec (for [[fixture row] (map vector fixtures results)\n                                  :when (and (= :pass (:status row))\n                                             (kernel-executed-arity? row symbol n)\n                                             (= symbol (first (:call fixture)))\n                                             (= n (count (rest (:call fixture)))))]\n                              (:id fixture)))\n                integration (vec (for [row results\n                                       :when (and (= :pass (:status row))\n                                                  (contains? kernel-named-integrations (:id row))\n                                                  (kernel-executed-arity? row symbol n))]\n                                   (:id row)))]]\n      {:function-arity [symbol n]\n       :exercise (cond (seq direct) :direct\n                       (seq integration) :named-integration\n                       :else :unexercised)\n       :direct-fixture-ids direct\n       :integration-fixture-ids integration\n       :missing-dependency (when (and (empty? direct) (empty? integration))\n                             (get kernel-unexercised-reasons [symbol n]\n                                  \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\"))})))\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-declarations\n  \"The declared dispositions: explicit, versioned input to classification.\n   Generated evidence is never their source of truth; provenance is in-file.\n   The file's contract is validated at load: version and provenance are\n   fixed, and every historical disposition must retain its exact boundary\n   and a complete record - the file is authoritative for this metadata, and\n   a load-time failure means the file was edited beyond its contract. A\n   declaration whose revalidation guards fail leaves its row a blocker,\n   not a deviation.\"\n  (let [parsed (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn\")))\n        complete? (fn [d required] (every? d required))\n        portability-required [:call :script :message :boundary :upstream-value :reason]\n        upstream-required [:call :boundary :reason :upstream-revision]]\n    (assert (and (= 3 (:version parsed))\n                 (= \"004246b48ddac39e0ecd3631a16f4e74b05cab7a\" (:provenance parsed)))\n            \"the declarations file's version/provenance are part of its contract\")\n    (doseq [[id d] (:portability parsed)]\n      (assert (and (complete? d portability-required)\n                   (= :nonportable-host-value (:boundary d))\n                   (= 'clojure.core/meta (:upstream-value d)))\n              (str \"incomplete or out-of-scope portability declaration: \" id)))\n    (doseq [[id d] (:upstream-failures parsed)]\n      (assert (and (complete? d upstream-required)\n                   (= (:boundary d) ({:typing-ascription :upstream-unbound-definition\n                                      :compile-malformed :upstream-malformed-proof-sequence} id))\n                   (= \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\" (:upstream-revision d)))\n              (str \"incomplete or out-of-scope upstream-failure declaration: \" id)))\n    parsed))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-callable-descriptor?\n  \"True when `value` is the shape of the admitted common-call descriptor the\n\n(deftest test-kernel-acceptance-counting\n  (let [inventory [{:symbol 'latte-kernel.syntax/subst :arities [2 3] :disposition :admitted}\n                   {:symbol 'latte-kernel.syntax/term? :arities [1] :disposition :admitted}]\n        fixture {:id :direct-subst :call '(latte-kernel.syntax/subst x y)}\n        calls '[[gate-syntax-subst 2 1]]\n        rows [{:id :direct-subst :status :pass\n               :c-walker {:executed-calls calls} :c-semantic {:executed-calls calls}}\n              {:id :check-assume-have-discharge :status :pass\n               :included-functions ['gate-syntax-subst]\n               :c-walker {:executed-calls calls} :c-semantic {:executed-calls calls}}]\n        entries (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture] rows)]\n    (is (= [:direct :unexercised :unexercised] (mapv :exercise entries))\n        \"An admitted but uncalled arity stays uncredited despite static membership\")\n    (is (empty? (:integration-fixture-ids (second entries))))\n    (is (= [:unexercised :unexercised :unexercised]\n           (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture]\n                                                    (mapv #(assoc % :status :mismatch) rows)))))\n    (let [observed (mapv #(-> %\n                              (assoc-in [:c-walker :executed-calls] '[[gate-syntax-subst 2 1] [gate-syntax-subst 3 2]])\n                              (assoc-in [:c-semantic :executed-calls] '[[gate-syntax-subst 2 1] [gate-syntax-subst 3 2]])) rows)]\n      (is (= [:direct :named-integration :unexercised]\n             (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture] observed))))\n      (is (= [:direct :named-integration :unexercised]\n             (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture]\n                                                      (mapv #(dissoc % :included-functions) observed)))))\n      (is (= [:direct :unexercised :unexercised]\n             (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture]\n                                                      (assoc-in observed [1 :id] :unnamed-integration))))))\n    (doseq [lane [:c-walker :c-semantic]]\n      (is (= [:unexercised :unexercised :unexercised]\n             (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture]\n                                                      (mapv #(dissoc % lane) rows))))\n          \"Both C lanes must demonstrate the exact arity\")))\n  (let [script (vector [:qed '(lambda [A :type] (lambda [x A] x)) {}] [:qed 'missing {}])\n        declared-call (get-in kernel-declarations [:portability :elab-after-qed :call])\n        fixture {:id :elab-after-qed :call declared-call}]\n    (is (= (vec (:script (get-in kernel-declarations [:portability :elab-after-qed]))) (vec script))\n        \"The controls model the declared script exactly\")\n    (let [a {:status :completed\n             :outcome {:thrown {:message \"Wrong proof script: proof steps after qed.\"\n                                :data {:script script\n                                       :meta {:nonportable-host-value (str (class clojure.core/meta))}}}}}\n          descriptor {:yang.call/entry (values/closure nil {})\n                      :clj/type :function\n                      :clj/outcomes? true\n                      :clj/admission (values/closure nil {})}\n          c-with (fn [meta]\n                   {:status :completed\n                    :outcome [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"Wrong proof script: proof steps after qed.\"\n                                            :yin.k/data {:script script :meta meta}}]})]\n      ;; Both representations the reconciled pipeline actually produces.\n      (is (some? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n                                              (c-with (values/closure nil {})) (c-with (values/closure nil {})))))\n      (is (some? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor)))\n          \"The admitted §8.10 descriptor classifies as the declared deviation\")\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation (assoc fixture :id :other) a a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor))))\n      ;; The declared-call pin: a mutated call refuses.\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation (assoc fixture :call '(latte-kernel.proof/elab-proof env [] (quote [[:qed :wrong]])))\n                                             a a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor)))\n          \"a mutated call fails the declared-call pin\")\n      ;; Per-lane incompleteness: each of the four executions must be complete.\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture (assoc a :status :blocked) a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor))))\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a (assoc a :status :blocked) (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor))))\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (assoc (c-with descriptor) :status :blocked) (c-with descriptor))))\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with descriptor) (assoc (c-with descriptor) :status :blocked))))\n      ;; Payload and shape mutations refuse.\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n                                             (assoc-in (c-with descriptor) [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data :script] [:new-mismatch])\n                                             (c-with descriptor))))\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n                                             (assoc-in (c-with descriptor) [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data :script] '())\n                                             (c-with descriptor))))\n      ;; Shape-only mutation: identical contents delivered as a list in A\n      ;; while the declaration (and C) keep the vector - the vec-normalized\n      ;; declaration guard alone would accept it, and the refusal lands on\n      ;; the A=B outcome equality (and, had B agreed, the raw shape\n      ;; comparison) - both layers hold.\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture\n                                             (assoc-in a [:outcome :thrown :data :script]\n                                                       (apply list script))\n                                             a\n                                             (c-with descriptor)\n                                             (c-with descriptor))))\n      ;; Descriptor forgeries refuse.\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n                                             (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/admission))\n                                             (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/admission))))\n          \"a descriptor without its admission witness fails\")\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :yang.call/entry :not-a-closure))\n                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :yang.call/entry :not-a-closure))))\n          \"a descriptor whose entry is not a minted closure fails\")\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :clj/type :data))\n                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :clj/type :data))))\n          \"a descriptor with a wrong type marker fails\")\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :clj/outcomes? false))\n                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :clj/outcomes? false))))\n          \"a descriptor with a false outcomes marker fails\")\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n                                             (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/outcomes?))\n                                             (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/outcomes?))))\n          \"a descriptor with a missing outcomes marker fails\")\n      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with {:type :closure}) (c-with {:type :closure}))))\n      ;; A descriptor copied across calls: the structurally valid\n      ;; check-after-qed descriptor submitted under the elab-after-qed\n      ;; fixture refuses through the declared-call pin - the copy carries\n      ;; another call's identity. (Two descriptors of the SAME call with\n      ;; identical payloads are the same deviation claim; their witness\n      ;; authenticity is the compiler's admission check.)\n      (is (nil? (let [other (get-in kernel-declarations [:portability :check-after-qed])\n                      other-descriptor (assoc descriptor :yang.call/entry (values/closure nil {})\n                                              :clj/admission (values/closure nil {}))]\n                  (kernel-host-value-deviation (assoc fixture :call (:call other))\n                                               a a (c-with other-descriptor) (c-with other-descriptor))))\n          \"a descriptor copied across calls fails the declared-call pin\")\n      ;; A mutated declaration (declared message != live failure) fails the guard.\n      (with-redefs [kernel-declarations (assoc-in kernel-declarations\n                                                  [:portability :elab-after-qed :message]\n                                                  \"A different declared failure\")]\n        (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor))))\n        \"carrying a declaration forward means revalidating it, not copying it\"))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-row\n  [fixture]\n  (let [a (kernel-a fixture)\n        b (kernel-b fixture)\n        compiled (kernel-attempt #(kernel-compile fixture))\n        compiled (if (and (= :blocked (:status compiled)) (not (:blocked-by compiled)))\n                   (assoc compiled :phase :compile\n                          :blocked-by (if-let [n (get-in compiled [:data :name])] [n] [:compiler-exception])\n                          :minimal-source (get kernel-sources (get-in compiled [:data :name]))) compiled)\n        walker (kernel-c compiled :walker)\n        semantic (kernel-c compiled :semantic)\n        match? (and (= :completed (:status a) (:status b) (:status walker) (:status semantic))\n                    (= (:outcome a) (:outcome b))\n                    (agrees? (get a :outcome) (get walker :outcome))\n                    (= (:outcome walker) (:outcome semantic))\n                    (= (result-shape (:outcome a)) (result-shape (:outcome b)))\n                    (if (contains? (:outcome a) :value)\n                      (= (result-shape (:value (:outcome a)))\n                         (result-shape (second (:outcome walker))))\n                      (= (result-shape (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :data]))\n                         (result-shape (get-in walker [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data])))))\n        deviation (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a b walker semantic)\n        upstream-failure (kernel-upstream-failure fixture a b walker semantic)\n        status (cond match? :pass\n                     upstream-failure :recorded-upstream-failure\n                     (some #(= :blocked (:status %)) [a b walker semantic]) :blocked\n                     deviation :recorded-deviation\n                     :else :mismatch)]\n    {:id (:id fixture) :mode (:mode fixture) :negative? (boolean (:negative? fixture)) :status status\n     :recorded-deviation deviation\n     :recorded-upstream-failure upstream-failure\n     :dependency-of (:dependency-of fixture)\n     :call (or (:call fixture) (kernel-c-program fixture))\n     :adapted-call (:guest-call fixture)\n     :site-table (:site-table compiled)\n     :site-table-hash (:site-table-hash compiled)\n     :canonical-source-hash (:canonical-source-hash compiled)\n     :agreement {:a-b (and (= :completed (:status a) (:status b)) (= (:outcome a) (:outcome b)))\n                 :a-c-walker (and (= :completed (:status a) (:status walker))\n                                  (agrees? (:outcome a) (:outcome walker)))\n                 :a-c-semantic (and (= :completed (:status a) (:status semantic))\n                                    (agrees? (:outcome a) (:outcome semantic)))\n                 :c-lanes (and (= :completed (:status walker) (:status semantic))\n                               (= (:outcome walker) (:outcome semantic)))}\n     :a a :b b :c-walker walker :c-semantic semantic\n     :included-functions (mapv second (kernel-closure (kernel-c-program fixture)))}))\n\n\n(deftest test-kernel-unused-arity-execution\n  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :parse-to-normalize-to-type (:id %)) (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus)))\n        fname 'gate-presyntax-parse\n        source (get kernel-sources fname)\n        ;; Preserve parse/2; poison the uncalled parse/1 body in memory.\n        poisoned (list* 'defn fname\n                        (map (fn [arity]\n                               (if (= 1 (count (first arity)))\n                                 (list (first arity) '(throw (ex-info \"Uncalled parse/1 entered\" {})))\n                                 arity)) (drop 2 source)))\n        row (with-redefs [kernel-sources (assoc kernel-sources fname poisoned)]\n              (kernel-row fixture))\n        inventory [{:symbol 'latte-kernel.presyntax/parse :arities [1 2] :disposition :admitted}]\n        entries (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture] [row])]\n    (is (= :pass (:status row)))\n    (is (some #{fname} (:included-functions row)) \"Both arities remain in the static closure\")\n    (doseq [lane [:c-walker :c-semantic]]\n      (is (some #(= [fname 2] (butlast %)) (get-in row [lane :executed-calls])))\n      (is (not-any? #(= [fname 1] (butlast %)) (get-in row [lane :executed-calls]))))\n    (is (= [:unexercised :named-integration] (mapv :exercise entries)))\n    (is (empty? (:integration-fixture-ids (first entries))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-h3-2-proof-elaboration-family\n(deftest test-attribution-battery\n  \"The ruling's seven-case refusal battery plus the stale-table\n   diagnostic (R2b), each case a real executed check of the ruled\n   attribution over caller-site-tagged traces.\"\n  (let [by-id (fn [id] (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus))))\n        f2 (kernel-row (by-id :h3-3-registered-definition-ambient))\n        explicit-2 (kernel-row {:id :battery-explicit-2\n                                :call '(latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition?\n                                         env (quote gate-no-such-definition))})\n        unexecuted-1 (kernel-row {:id :battery-unexecuted-ambient\n                                  :call '(if false\n                                           (latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition?\n                                             (quote gate-no-such-definition))\n                                           (latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition?\n                                             env (quote gate-no-such-definition)))})]\n    (testing \"case 1: an explicit /2 call supplying an empty environment does not credit /1\"\n      (is (= :pass (:status explicit-2)))\n      ;; the supplied context VALUE is the empty environment — value-identical\n      ;; to the ambient initialization; the shapes are disjoint\n      (is (kernel-executed-arity? explicit-2 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 2)\n          \"the explicit context shape credits /2\")\n      (is (not (kernel-executed-arity? explicit-2 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n          \"no value equality borrows /1 credit\"))\n    (testing \"case 2: an unexecuted ambient /1 beside an executed explicit /2 borrows nothing\"\n      (is (= :pass (:status unexecuted-1)))\n      (is (kernel-executed-arity? unexecuted-1 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 2)\n          \"the executed explicit call credits /2\")\n      (is (not (kernel-executed-arity? unexecuted-1 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n          \"the ambient site exists in the table but was never entered\"))\n    (testing \"case 3: mismatched program/adaptation evidence refuses\"\n      (let [r2 (kernel-row (by-id :h3-3-registered-definition-nonsymbol))\n            swapped (assoc f2 :canonical-source-hash (:canonical-source-hash r2))]\n        (is (not (kernel-executed-arity? swapped 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n            \"a trace read against another fixture's canonical-source-hash refuses\")))\n    (testing \"case 4: missing-lane evidence refuses\"\n      (let [one-lane (assoc-in f2 [:c-semantic :executed-calls] [])]\n        (is (kernel-executed-arity? f2 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n        (is (not (kernel-executed-arity? one-lane 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n            \"both C lanes must record the entry\")))\n    (testing \"case 5: a site declared ambient whose compiled argument is not the ambient literal refuses\"\n      (let [table (:site-table f2)\n            ambient (some (fn [[k s]]\n                            (when (and (= 'registered-definition? (:callee s))\n                                       (= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes s))))\n                              k))\n                          table)\n            ;; the explicit fixture's adapted /2 threads the caller's\n            ;; context argument as a parameter expression — statically\n            ;; NOT the ambient literal, whatever value it holds\n            variable-site (some (fn [[k s]]\n                                  (when (and (= 'registered-definition? (:callee s))\n                                             (seq (:arg-shapes s))\n                                             (not= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes s))))\n                                    k))\n                                (:site-table explicit-2))]\n        (is (some? ambient) \"the fixture really derives an ambient site\")\n        (is (kernel-ambient-site? table ambient))\n        (is (some? variable-site) \"the fixture really derives parameter-shaped sites\")\n        (is (not (kernel-ambient-site? (:site-table explicit-2) variable-site))\n            \"the compile-time verification refuses a non-literal argument\")))\n    (testing \"case 6: indirect-origin body entries refuse\"\n      (let [table (:site-table f2)\n            dynamic (some (fn [[k s]] (when (= :dynamic (:callee s)) k)) table)\n            none-site ['gate-defenv-registered-definition? 1 :gate-site/none]]\n        (is (not (kernel-record-credits? none-site table\n                                         'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n            \"an entry without a stamped caller site never credits\")\n        (when dynamic\n          (is (not (kernel-record-credits? ['registered-definition? 3 dynamic] table\n                                           'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n              \"an entry through an indirect site refuses unless site-linked\"))))\n    (testing \"case 7: a variable context argument is /2-only, never ambient\"\n      (let [table (:site-table explicit-2)\n            variable-site (some (fn [[k s]]\n                                  (when (and (= 'registered-definition? (:callee s))\n                                             (seq (:arg-shapes s))\n                                             (not= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes s))))\n                                    k))\n                                table)]\n        (is (some? variable-site)\n            \"the explicit fixture really derives a variable context argument\")\n        (is (not (kernel-ambient-site? table variable-site)))\n        (is (not (kernel-record-credits? ['registered-definition? 3 variable-site] table\n                                         'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n            \"the statically unclassifiable shape defaults to refusal\")))\n    (testing \"case 8: a stale table is a recorded diagnostic, not silent non-credit\"\n      (let [table (:site-table f2)\n            stale-table (-> table\n                            (dissoc 5)\n                            (assoc 999 {:site 999 :callee 'registered-definition?\n                                        :arg-shapes [:ambient-literal] :def nil\n                                        :delegation? false}))\n            stale (kernel-stale-sites stale-table {:c-walker (:c-walker f2)\n                                                   :c-semantic (:c-semantic f2)})]\n        (is (contains? (set stale) 999)\n            \"the mistyped site id is reported, never silently ignored\")\n        (is (vector? stale) \"the diagnostic is recorded data\")))))\n\n\n(defn kernel-gate-evidence\n  \"Run every fixture in A and independently in both C lanes. Compilation or\n   VM errors are blockers, never successful LaTTe rejections. Exact arities\n   require recorded body entry in both C lanes of a passing fixture.\"\n  []\n  (let [results (mapv (fn [fixture]\n                        (let [row (kernel-row fixture)]\n                          (println \"KERNEL-FIXTURE\" (:id row) (:status row))\n                          row)) (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus))\n        inventory (mapv #(select-keys % [:symbol :kind :arities :disposition :admission-reason]) kernel-entries)\n        exercise-entries (kernel-exercise-entries inventory (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus) results)\n        direct (set (map :function-arity (filter #(= :direct (:exercise %)) exercise-entries)))\n        exercised (set (map :function-arity (remove #(= :unexercised (:exercise %)) exercise-entries)))\n        all-arities (set (for [{:keys [symbol arities]} inventory n arities] [symbol n]))\n        admitted-arities (set (for [{:keys [symbol arities disposition]} inventory\n                                    :when (= :admitted disposition) n arities] [symbol n]))\n        unexercised (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove exercised admitted-arities)))]\n    {:slice 9 :gate-status (if (and (every? #(contains? #{:pass :recorded-deviation :recorded-upstream-failure} (:status %)) results)\n                                    (empty? unexercised)) :pass :blocked)\n     :baseline {:revision \"7dc18478\" :fixture-count 54 :counts {:pass 4 :mismatch 2 :blocked 48}}\n     :generated-at (str (java.time.Instant/now))\n     :adaptation-version {:context 2 :kernel-assembly 4}\n     :executions {:a :original-upstream-clojure :b :context-source-clojure\n                  :c [:walker :semantic]}\n     :upstream-revision \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"\n     :compiler-vm-revision {:base \"7dc18478\" :working-tree true}\n     :compiler-source-sha256\n     (apply str (map #(format \"%02x\" (bit-and 255 %))\n                     (.digest (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \"SHA-256\")\n                              (.getBytes (slurp \"src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\") \"UTF-8\"))))\n     :integration-context-identities kernel-context-integration-names\n     :portability-refusals\n     [{:source '(.getStackTrace exc) :disposition :excluded\n       :reason \"Host stack traces have no portable error-data representation; the compiler refuses the accessor.\"}]\n     :representation-seams\n     {'kind/var? \"JVM Clojure Var predicate; explicitly declared, with no namespace lookup.\"\n      'kind/with-meta \"Pure metadata attachment on the existing host value representation; the data ABI has no metadata-write export.\"}\n     :context-fields {'latte-kernel.proof/+opacity-fn+ :opacity-policy}\n     :fresh-supply-convention\n     {:input {:counter 0} :allocation '(gensym supply prefix)\n      :result '[symbol next-supply]\n      :rebuild-type-result '[original-result next-context]\n      :ambient-prefix-only :refused}\n     :runtime {:clojure (clojure-version) :java (System/getProperty \"java.version\")}\n     :instruction-budget-per-lane 4000000\n     :instruction-budget-note \"The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions. Body-entry stream writes add guest instructions; traced fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound. The harness drains only after halt. Under the D2 record lane the binding fixture's walker cell needs 2,024,912 steps (1.2% over 2M; semantic 1,105,792); the architect's 2026-11-04 ruling approves a uniform 4,000,000 acceptance budget (~1.98x headroom on the binding lane, measurement-supported, no per-fixture table). The attribution round's caller-site stamping adds one dispatcher call and one cell write per stamped guest call; every fixture in this evidence completed under the same 4,000,000 bound with the stamping active, and the trace stream bound stays stream/make 1000000 (one added field per body-entry record, no added records).\"\n     :manifest-bindings (count manifest) :function-arity-candidates (count all-arities)\n     :manifest-functions (count (filter :arities kernel-entries))\n     :admitted-function-arity-count (count admitted-arities)\n     :excluded-function-arity-count (- (count all-arities) (count admitted-arities))\n     :binding-dispositions (frequencies (map :disposition manifest))\n     :admission-note \"Manifest dispositions define the denominator independently of fixture success; excluded bindings retain explicit portability reasons.\"\n     :program-status (if (empty? unexercised) :fixture-closure-complete :execution-evidence-incomplete)\n     :residual-closure kernel-fixture-closure\n     :coverage {:proven-direct-function-arities (vec (sort-by pr-str direct))\n                :exercised-count (count exercised) :unexercised unexercised\n                :entries exercise-entries\n                :named-integration-fixture-ids (vec (sort kernel-named-integrations))\n                :transitive-execution-coverage :recorded-function-arity-body-entry\n                :attribution-at-rule kernel-ambient-correspondence\n                :trace {:record-shape '[guest-function arity caller-site]\n                        :transport :explicit-guest-stream :lanes [:c-walker :c-semantic]\n                        :point :selected-arity-body-entry\n                        :site-tagging :caller-side-compiled-ast-application\n                        :refusal-site :gate-site/none}\n                :basis \"Passing direct calls or named integrations must record the exact function/arity executing in both C lanes. Static closure membership never counts; full branch coverage is not required.\"\n                :inventory inventory}\n     :recorded-portability-boundaries\n     (mapv #(select-keys % [:id :status :recorded-deviation])\n           (filter #(= :recorded-deviation (:status %)) results))\n     :recorded-upstream-failures\n     (mapv #(select-keys % [:id :status :recorded-upstream-failure])\n           (filter #(= :recorded-upstream-failure (:status %)) results))\n     :attribution\n     {:version 1\n      :rule \"caller-side site ids at compiled-AST application expressions (post-macroexpansion); records [guest-function arity caller-site]; ambient arities credit only through adapter-declared ambient-literal sites; delegations and the :gate-site/none entry site never credit\"\n      :ambient-correspondence kernel-ambient-correspondence\n      :site-tables-file \"slice9_site_tables.edn\"\n      :stale-site-diagnostics\n      (into (sorted-map)\n            (for [row results\n                  :let [stale (kernel-stale-sites (:site-table row)\n                                                  {:c-walker (:c-walker row)\n                                                   :c-semantic (:c-semantic row)})]\n                  :when (and (seq stale) (= :pass (:status row)))]\n              [(:id row) stale]))}\n     :counts (frequencies (map :status results)) :fixture-count (count results)\n     :negative-fixture-count (count (filter :negative? results))\n     :dependency-graph\n     (into (sorted-map)\n           (for [[fname source] kernel-sources]\n             [fname (vec (sort (filter (set (keys kernel-sources)) (walk-symbols source))))]))\n     ;; the derived site tables stay on the rows (the query re-derives\n     ;; credit from them); the evidence writer omits them from the\n     ;; inline rows and lands them in the versioned companion file\n     :fixtures results}))\n\n\n(defn write-kernel-gate-evidence!\n  \"Explicit evidence/coverage refresh; normal tests never update these files.\n   With `dir`, writes into that directory (the round-trip test's temp dir);\n   without it, the checked-in locations.\"\n  ([] (write-kernel-gate-evidence! \"test/yang/latte_oracle\"))\n  ([dir]\n   (let [evidence (kernel-gate-evidence)]\n     (spit (str dir \"/slice9_unexercised.edn\")\n           (str \";; GENERATED from exact execution evidence in both C lanes.\\n\"\n                (pr-str (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (pr-str %1) (pr-str %2)))\n                              (for [entry (get-in evidence [:coverage :entries])\n                                    :when (= :unexercised (:exercise entry))]\n                                [(:function-arity entry) (:missing-dependency entry)]))) \"\\n\"))\n     ;; The versioned site tables (R1b/R7): one derived table and one\n     ;; canonical-source-hash per fixture, stable across refreshes so the\n     ;; later durable correspondence record lands additively.\n     (spit (str dir \"/slice9_site_tables.edn\")\n           (str \";; GENERATED from the compiled AST of each fixture's C program.\\n\"\n                (pr-str {:version 1\n                         :fixtures\n                         (into (sorted-map)\n                               (for [row (:fixtures evidence)]\n                                 [(:id row)\n                                  {:canonical-source-hash (:canonical-source-hash row)\n                                   :site-table (:site-table row)}]))})\n                \"\\n\"))\n     (with-open [w (io/writer (str dir \"/slice9_evidence.edn\"))]\n       ;; prn keeps (quote ...) in valid EDN rather than pprint's reader\n       ;; shorthand. One fixture per line keeps refreshes independently diffable.\n       (binding [*out* w *print-length* nil *print-level* nil]\n         (print \"{\")\n         (doseq [[k v] (dissoc evidence :fixtures)] (pr k) (print \" \") (prn v))\n         (println \":fixtures [\")\n         (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)] (prn (dissoc row :site-table)))\n         (println \"]}\")))\n     (select-keys evidence [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates :coverage :attribution]))))\n\n\n(deftest test-kernel-differential-gate\n  (let [evidence (kernel-gate-evidence)]\n    (is (= (count (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus)) (count (set (map :id (:fixtures evidence)))))\n        \"Every named fixture runs exactly once, including negatives\")\n    (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)\n            :when (and (:negative? row) (= :completed (get-in row [:a :status])))\n            :let [outcome (get-in row [:a :outcome]) value (:value outcome)\n                  fixture (first (filter #(= (:id row) (:id %)) (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus)))]]\n      (is (or (:thrown outcome) (false? value) (and (sequential? value) (= :ko (first value)))\n              (and (:refusal-path fixture) (false? (get-in outcome (:refusal-path fixture)))))\n          (str \"A must actually reject the named negative: \" (:id row))))\n    (is (= (:function-arity-candidates evidence)\n           (+ (:admitted-function-arity-count evidence) (:excluded-function-arity-count evidence)))\n        \"Admitted and excluded arities partition the candidate inventory\")\n    (is (every? #(every? true? (vals (:agreement %)))\n                (filter #(= :pass (:status %)) (:fixtures evidence)))\n        \"Every passing fixture records independent A/B/C agreement\")\n    (let [entries (get-in evidence [:coverage :entries])\n          unexercised (filter #(= :unexercised (:exercise %)) entries)\n          deviations (filter #(= :recorded-deviation (:status %)) (:fixtures evidence))]\n      (is (= (:admitted-function-arity-count evidence) (count entries)\n             (count (set (map :function-arity entries)))))\n      (is (= (set (get-in evidence [:coverage :unexercised]))\n             (set (map :function-arity unexercised))\n             (set (keys kernel-unexercised-reasons))))\n      (is (every? #(seq (:missing-dependency %)) unexercised))\n      (is (every? #(case (:exercise %)\n                     :direct (seq (:direct-fixture-ids %))\n                     :named-integration (seq (:integration-fixture-ids %))\n                     :unexercised (and (empty? (:direct-fixture-ids %))\n                                       (empty? (:integration-fixture-ids %)))) entries))\n      (doseq [{[symbol n] :function-arity :keys [direct-fixture-ids integration-fixture-ids]} entries\n              id (concat direct-fixture-ids integration-fixture-ids)\n              :let [row (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) (:fixtures evidence)))]]\n        (is (= :pass (:status row)))\n        (is (kernel-executed-arity? row symbol n)\n            (str \"Every credited path re-derives from both execution traces: \" [symbol n id])))\n      (is (= #{:elab-after-qed :check-after-qed} (set (map :id deviations))))\n      (is (every? #(and (:recorded-deviation %)\n                        (not (every? true? (vals (:agreement %))))) deviations)))\n    (testing \"Previously declared residual consumers must still prove their exact arities\"\n      (is (= 20 (count kernel-fixture-closure)))\n      (doseq [[arity {:keys [fixture expected] :as closure}] kernel-fixture-closure\n              :let [row (first (filter #(= fixture (:id %)) (:fixtures evidence)))\n                    entry (first (filter #(= arity (:function-arity %)) (get-in evidence [:coverage :entries])))]]\n        (is (= :pass (:status row)) (str arity \" via \" fixture))\n        (is (some #{fixture} (concat (:direct-fixture-ids entry) (:integration-fixture-ids entry)))\n            (str \"Primary consumer must contribute to arity evidence: \" arity))\n        (is (contains? closure :expected))\n        (is (= {:value expected} (get-in row [:a :outcome])) (str fixture \" has the intended result\"))))\n    (is (= #{:typing-ascription :compile-malformed}\n           (set (map :id (:recorded-upstream-failures evidence)))))\n    (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)\n            :when (= :recorded-upstream-failure (:status row))\n            :let [fixture (first (filter #(= (:id row) (:id %)) (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus)))]]\n      (is (:recorded-upstream-failure row))\n      (is (not (every? true? (vals (:agreement row)))))\n      (is (nil? (kernel-upstream-failure (assoc fixture :id :unexpected)\n                                         (:a row) (:b row) (:c-walker row) (:c-semantic row))))\n      (is (nil? (kernel-upstream-failure (assoc fixture :call '(changed-input))\n                                         (:a row) (:b row) (:c-walker row) (:c-semantic row))))\n      (is (nil? (kernel-upstream-failure fixture (:a row) (:b row)\n                                         (assoc-in (:c-walker row) [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data] {:changed true})\n                                         (:c-semantic row)))))\n    (println \"KERNEL-GATE\" (pr-str (select-keys evidence [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates\n                                                          :recorded-portability-boundaries :recorded-upstream-failures])))\n    (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence) :when (not= :pass (:status row))]\n      (println (case (:status row)\n                 :recorded-deviation \"KERNEL-RECORDED-BOUNDARY\"\n                 :recorded-upstream-failure \"KERNEL-RECORDED-UPSTREAM-FAILURE\"\n                 \"KERNEL-BLOCKER\")\n               (pr-str {:id (:id row) :status (:status row)\n                        :blocked-by (get-in row [:c-walker :blocked-by])\n                        :a (get-in row [:a :status]) :b (get-in row [:b :status])\n                        :c-walker (get-in row [:c-walker :status])\n                        :c-semantic (get-in row [:c-semantic :status])})))\n    (is (= :pass (:gate-status evidence))\n        (str \"Kernel gate remains blocked: \" (:counts evidence)\n             \"; admitted/candidate but unexercised function/arities=\" (count (get-in evidence [:coverage :unexercised]))\n             \". See slice9_evidence.edn; blocked fixtures are not accepted negatives.\"))))\n\n\n(deftest test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip\n  \"Rewriting the checked-in evidence through the writer into a temporary\n   directory reproduces it exactly: the statuses (including the declared\n   deviations), the raw comparisons and the coverage survive. No fixtures\n   re-run; the checked-in file is the fixture.\"\n  (let [dir (str (System/getProperty \"java.io.tmpdir\") \"/slice9-roundtrip-\" (System/currentTimeMillis))\n        committed (edn/read-string (slurp \"test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn\"))]\n    (try\n      (.mkdirs (java.io.File. dir))\n      (with-redefs [kernel-gate-evidence (constantly committed)]\n        (write-kernel-gate-evidence! dir))\n      (let [written (edn/read-string (slurp (str dir \"/slice9_evidence.edn\")))]\n        (is (= committed written) \"the writer's output re-reads as the same evidence\")\n        (is (= #{:elab-after-qed :check-after-qed}\n               (set (map :id (filter #(= :recorded-deviation (:status %)) (:fixtures written)))))\n            \"the declared departures survive as recorded deviations\")\n        (is (every? (fn [row]\n                      (and (contains? row :a) (contains? row :b)\n                           (contains? row :c-walker) (contains? row :c-semantic)))\n                    (:fixtures written))\n            \"every fixture row keeps its raw A/B/C comparisons\")\n        (let [unexercised (edn/read-string (slurp (str dir \"/slice9_unexercised.edn\")))]\n          (is (= (count (get-in written [:coverage :unexercised])) (count unexercised))\n              \"the companion file lists every unexercised arity with its dependency\"))\n        (let [tables (edn/read-string (slurp (str dir \"/slice9_site_tables.edn\")))]\n          (is (= 1 (:version tables)) \"the site tables land in the versioned format\")\n          (is (= (count (:fixtures written)) (count (:fixtures tables)))\n              \"every fixture row carries its derived site table and canonical-source-hash\")))\n      (finally\n        (run! #(let [f (java.io.File. (str dir \"/\" %))] (when (.exists f) (.delete f)))\n              [\"slice9_evidence.edn\" \"slice9_unexercised.edn\" \"slice9_site_tables.edn\"])\n        (let [d (java.io.File. dir)] (when (.exists d) (.delete d)))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '3056,3107p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '124,129p' deps.edn; tail -70 test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md; command -v clojure; command -v java; rg -n 'H3-6|caveat|Case.3|case.6' collab/yang-clojure/*aaq* collab/yang-clojure/*h3-6*\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '3056,3107p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '124,129p' deps.edn; tail -70 test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md; command -v clojure; command -v java; rg -n 'H3-6|caveat|Case.3|case.6' collab/yang-clojure/*aaq* collab/yang-clojure/*h3-6*\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.latte-oracle-test\n  \"Pinned upstream LaTTe differential harness, slices 1-9 of the Yang gap\n   program. A executes the original library on Clojure. B executes explicit\n   portability source on Clojure; C compiles it through Yang for the walker\n   and semantic VMs. Slice 9 fails closed on the full kernel corpus. The\n   legacy classifier records historical blockers;\n   the context module additionally checks free-symbol admission before C.\n   Adaptations, operation sequences and scope departures live beside the\n   manifest in yang/latte_oracle/.\"\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [clojure.tools.reader :as r]\n            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rows-support]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n\n\n(def ^:private manifest\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- ns-declaration-aliases\n  \"Alias -> full ns symbol, taken from the file's own (ns ...) declaration —\n   never invented: ::alias/kw must read as :that.real.ns/kw.\"\n  [ns-form]\n  (let [alias-map (atom {})\n        consume-spec (fn [spec]\n                       (when (sequential? spec)\n                         (let [lib (first spec)]\n                           (loop [xs (rest spec)]\n                             (when (seq xs)\n                               (if (= :as (first xs))\n                                 (do (swap! alias-map assoc (second xs) lib)\n                                     (recur (drop 2 xs)))\n                                 (recur (next xs))))))))]\n    (loop [clauses (rest (rest ns-form))]\n      (when (seq clauses)\n        (let [clause (first clauses)]\n          (if (and (seq? clause) (= :require (first clause)))\n            (do (loop [reqs (next clause)]\n                  (let [spec (first reqs)]\n                    (when (and (not (nil? spec)) (not (keyword? spec)))\n                      (consume-spec spec)\n                      (recur (next reqs)))))\n                (recur (next clauses)))\n            (recur (next clauses))))))\n    @alias-map))\n\n\n(defn- read-forms\n  \"Read one latte-kernel source file with reader conditionals resolved for\n   :clj, ::alias/kw keywords resolved against the file's own ns declaration,\n   and ::kw resolved against the file's own namespace — so the C leg compiles\n   the same keyword identities the upstream A leg runs.\"\n  [ns-sym]\n  (let [f (io/resource (str (str/replace (name ns-sym) \".\" \"/\") \".cljc\"))\n        pr (rt/source-logging-push-back-reader (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader f)) 1 (str f))\n        ns-form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)\n        declared-name (second ns-form)\n        aliases (ns-declaration-aliases ns-form)]\n    (binding [r/*alias-map* aliases\n              *ns* (the-ns (create-ns declared-name))]\n      (loop [acc []]\n        (let [form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)]\n          (if (= form ::eof) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private all-forms\n  (into {} (map (fn [ns-sym] [ns-sym (read-forms ns-sym)])\n                (distinct (map :ns manifest)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private top-forms\n  (into {} (map (fn [{:keys [ns kind name]}]\n          \"the executed explicit call credits /2\")\n      (is (not (kernel-executed-arity? unexecuted-1 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n          \"the ambient site exists in the table but was never entered\"))\n    (testing \"case 3: mismatched program/adaptation evidence refuses\"\n      (let [r2 (kernel-row (by-id :h3-3-registered-definition-nonsymbol))\n            swapped (assoc f2 :canonical-source-hash (:canonical-source-hash r2))]\n        (is (not (kernel-executed-arity? swapped 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n            \"a trace read against another fixture's canonical-source-hash refuses\")))\n    (testing \"case 4: missing-lane evidence refuses\"\n      (let [one-lane (assoc-in f2 [:c-semantic :executed-calls] [])]\n        (is (kernel-executed-arity? f2 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n        (is (not (kernel-executed-arity? one-lane 'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n            \"both C lanes must record the entry\")))\n    (testing \"case 5: a site declared ambient whose compiled argument is not the ambient literal refuses\"\n      (let [table (:site-table f2)\n            ambient (some (fn [[k s]]\n                            (when (and (= 'registered-definition? (:callee s))\n                                       (= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes s))))\n                              k))\n                          table)\n            ;; the explicit fixture's adapted /2 threads the caller's\n            ;; context argument as a parameter expression — statically\n            ;; NOT the ambient literal, whatever value it holds\n            variable-site (some (fn [[k s]]\n                                  (when (and (= 'registered-definition? (:callee s))\n                                             (seq (:arg-shapes s))\n                                             (not= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes s))))\n                                    k))\n                                (:site-table explicit-2))]\n        (is (some? ambient) \"the fixture really derives an ambient site\")\n        (is (kernel-ambient-site? table ambient))\n        (is (some? variable-site) \"the fixture really derives parameter-shaped sites\")\n        (is (not (kernel-ambient-site? (:site-table explicit-2) variable-site))\n            \"the compile-time verification refuses a non-literal argument\")))\n    (testing \"case 6: indirect-origin body entries refuse\"\n      (let [table (:site-table f2)\n            dynamic (some (fn [[k s]] (when (= :dynamic (:callee s)) k)) table)\n            none-site ['gate-defenv-registered-definition? 1 :gate-site/none]]\n        (is (not (kernel-record-credits? none-site table\n                                         'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n            \"an entry without a stamped caller site never credits\")\n        (when dynamic\n          (is (not (kernel-record-credits? ['registered-definition? 3 dynamic] table\n                                           'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1))\n              \"an entry through an indirect site refuses unless site-linked\"))))\n    (testing \"case 7: a variable context argument is /2-only, never ambient\"\n      (let [table (:site-table explicit-2)\n            variable-site (some (fn [[k s]]\n                                  (when (and (= 'registered-definition? (:callee s))\n                                             (seq (:arg-shapes s))\n                                             (not= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes s))))\n                                    k))\n           :oracle {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\" \"test\"]\n                    :extra-deps {com.datomic/client-api {:mvn/version \"1.0.69\"}\n                                 ;; oracle backend: Datomic Local, in-process,\n                                 ;; run in docker/oracle (dev-scope only)\n                                 com.datomic/local {:mvn/version \"1.0.301\"}}}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n(stub mirroring, mode assemblies, the fixture-call `env` binding) vs\nsites authored inside corpus guest-calls, and `delegation?` marks the\ncontext layer's internal self-delegations (own site id, no credit).\nThe tables land in a new versioned evidence file\n(`slice9_site_tables.edn`, `:version 1`) with the per-fixture\ncanonical-source-hash of the assembled program (R2b case 3's referent:\na trace from a fixture whose recorded hash differs refuses). The\nattribution itself is a `dao.space.query/q` join over three relations\n(records, site table, correspondence) so the H3-6 audit re-runs the\nsame query (R7).\n\n## 6. The pin migration record (R5 — every revised pin, mechanical and semantic)\n\nMechanical shape updates (2-vector → 3-vector records), all in\n`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` unless noted:\n\n1. `kernel-trace-form`'s record emitter — `[fname n]` →\n   `[fname n (cell/get gate-site-slot)]` (the `[:variadic idx]` arity\n   encoding preserved).\n2. `kernel-executed-arity?` — the offset-table predicate → the ruled\n   query (site-linked, non-delegation, hash-matched, both C lanes).\n3. `test-kernel-acceptance-counting`'s synthetic literals —\n   `[[gate-syntax-subst 2]]` → `[[gate-syntax-subst 2 1]]`,\n   `[gate-syntax-subst 3]` → `[gate-syntax-subst 3 2]`.\n4. `test-kernel-unused-arity-execution`'s pins — `[fname 2]`/`[fname 1]`\n   record equality → `(= [fname n] (butlast record))`.\n5. The F3/F2 witness pins — 2-vector `contains?` → 3-vector records\n   carrying the stamped site ids.\n6. The evidence `:trace` declaration — `:record-shape\n   [guest-function arity]` → `[guest-function arity caller-site]` with\n   `:site-tagging` and `:refusal-site`.\n7. `slice9_evidence.edn` — fully regenerated (155 rows, 3-vector\n   executed-calls, the `:attribution` section, gate-status :pass).\n8. `slice9_unexercised.edn` — regenerated to `{}` (its single entry,\n   `[registered-definition? 1]`, is retired by the re-credit).\n\nSemantic revisions (superseded pins, revised on the record):\n\n9. `kernel_gate.edn` — the `:guest-call` overrides on\n   `:h3-3-registered-definition-ambient` (F2) and\n   `:h3-3-registered-definition-nonsymbol` (R2) are dropped: the C lane\n   now runs the adapted upstream /1 call; the old overrides pinned the\n   pre-ruling non-crediting adaptation.\n10. F2/R2's `/1` refusal pins — \"no mapping turns F2's bare traces into\n    upstream /1 credit\" and \"R2 likewise credits nothing\" — flip to\n    credit assertions: the ambient-shape execution credits\n    `registered-definition?` /1 (the ruling's re-credit).\n11. The \"F2 stays honestly non-crediting\" registration pin comment —\n    F2 now credits as a direct ambient fixture, never as a named\n    integration (`kernel-named-integrations` membership unchanged).\n12. The eight context-API arities credited pre-ruling by\n    integration-name+offset matching (`local-definitions` /1,\n    `register-definition` /2, `unparse-term-once` /3,\n    `unparse-term-rec` /3, `register-unparser!` /3,\n    `install-unfold-implicit!` /1, `is-opaque?` /1,\n    `install-opacity-function` /1) — their credit events tighten from\n    any-record-at-shifted-arity to site-linked, non-delegation records\n    of the derived `:context-shift`/`:context-copy` carriers (see §3's\n    resolution). No credited arity is withdrawn; no witness is forced.\n13. The by-design red pin `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))` — the\n    assertion is unchanged and PASSES for the first time (165/165\n    admitted arities exercised).\n\n## 5. What does NOT move\n\n`yin.vm` and `yang.clojure` sources are untouched. The differential\ngate's versioned attribution section lands in `slice9_gate.md` (R4);\n`yin.cic.spec` v1 is untouched. D2, `cell/authentic?`, the\nevidence-walk bounds, and the declarations file's contract are\nunaffected.\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/clojure/1.12.4.1602/bin/clojure\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/java/21.0.2/bin/java\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793952534437-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:4:# Task: H3-6 Independent Audit of LaTTe Kernel Gate Closure (Slice 9)\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793952534437-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:9:- Model: kimi-k3.1-pro | Assigned: 2026-11-06 15:08:50 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: Independent audit to verify 165/165 arity reconstruction from raw traces, independent site table derivation, and verification of recorded caveats per slice9_gate.md.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793952534437-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:24:3. Verify Kimi's three recorded non-blocking caveats from the final gate run:\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793952534437-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:25:   (a) Case-3 hash guard: verify that recomputing the canonical source hash on the recorded-EDN path properly triggers refusal when hashes diverge.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793952534437-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:36:If all audit criteria pass and the gate closure is sound, state \"Audit passed: 165/165 arities verified from raw traces; site tables and caveats confirmed.\"\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793953025937-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:4:# Task: H3-6 Independent Audit of LaTTe Kernel Gate Closure (Slice 9)\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793953025937-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:10:- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-11-06 15:17:05 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: Reassigned to Codex (gpt-6.1-sol) on Jupiter to complete the independent H3-6 audit per team.md.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793953025937-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:25:3. Verify Kimi's three recorded non-blocking caveats from the final gate run:\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793953025937-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:26:   (a) Case-3 hash guard: verify that recomputing the canonical source hash on the recorded-EDN path properly triggers refusal when hashes diverge.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793953025937-reviewer-h3-6-audit.prompt.md:39:If all audit criteria pass and the gate closure is sound, state \"Audit passed: 165/165 arities verified from raw traces; site tables and caveats confirmed.\"\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793953025937-reviewer-h3-6-audit.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md collab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Slice 9 kernel differential gate: execution evidence correction\\n\\n## Attribution section — version 1 (attribution-as-query ruling of record)\\n\\nThis section versions the executed-arity attribution contract per the signed\\nruling `1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md`\\n(v4) and its implementation round. The gate's credit rule is now a query\\nover caller-site-tagged execution records, not name+arity string matching.\\n\\n- **Records.** Every instrumented arity body appends\\n  `[guest-function arity caller-site]` to the fixture's guest stream at body\\n  entry. The caller site id is assigned at APPLICATION EXPRESSIONS in the\\n  compiled AST, post-macroexpansion (the corpus runs under macros; source\\n  tagging would miss expanded sites), by a harness-owned instrumentation\\n  pass (`kernel-stamp-sites`) that threads each stamped call's argument\\n  vector through a guest site cell so the callee's first body form reads\\n  the applying site. This is instantiation #1 of the site contract,\\n  harness-level per Addendum A; yin.vm and yang.clojure are untouched. The\\n  walker/semantic ingresses ingest the stamped program unchanged.\\n- **Site tables.** Mechanically derived from each fixture's compiled AST\\n  (`R7`): every stamped site's callee, per-argument shapes\\n  (`:ambient-literal`, `:literal`, `:variable`, `:computed`,\\n  `:dynamic-callee`), enclosing definition, and self-delegation mark —\\n  recorded in the versioned [`slice9_site_tables.edn`](slice9_site_tables.edn)\\n  (`:version 1`) with the per-fixture canonical-source-hash of the inlined\\n  adaptation (R2b case 3's referent: a trace read against a differing hash\\n  refuses).\\n- **The query.** An upstream function-arity is credited when both C lanes\\n  record (a) the arity-preserving guest definition's body entry at the same\\n  arity through any real site (the degenerate 1:1 path), or (b) a body\\n  entry of a derived correspondence carrier — the guest/context callable\\n  and arity the derived correspondence names (`:attribution\\n  :ambient-correspondence` in the evidence) — entered through a\\n  SITE-LINKED record: the site table's static callee at that site is the\\n  carrier itself, and the site is not a self-delegation. The derived\\n  correspondence has three kinds. An `:ambient-delegation` path (R3's\\n  disjointness pair, `registered-definition?` /1) additionally requires\\n  the site's compiled context argument to have resolved to the\\n  adapter-supplied ambient literal. `:context-shift` paths — the retired\\n  offset table's scope (R6): the kernel-first context callable that\\n  replaced the upstream env parameter at the same arity or was added at\\n  one fewer argument (unregister-unparser!/1, unparse/1,\\n  register-unparser!/2 and /3, install-unfold-implicit!/1,\\n  install-fundamental-unparsers!/0, install-opacity-function/1,\\n  register-definition /2 and /3, local-definitions /1, …) — and\\n  `:context-copy` paths (the verbatim integration copies is-opaque?,\\n  unparse-term-once/rec) thread the adapted state explicitly, so their\\n  witness is the site-linked body entry of the carrier, whatever context\\n  value the site threads; the ambient literal never borrows across kinds.\\n  The retired offset table `kernel-context-extra-arguments` (six\\n  hand-declared +1 shifts) is replaced by that derived correspondence;\\n  its full coverage list is recorded in\\n  [`attribution_inventory.md`](attribution_inventory.md).\\n- **Refusals.** The seven-case battery\\n  (`test-attribution-battery`) pins: explicit `/2` supplying an empty\\n  environment never credits `/1` (disjointness by site identity and\\n  compiled argument shape, never value equality); unexecuted ambient sites\\n  borrow nothing; mismatched canonical-source-hash refuses; a missing lane\\n  refuses; a site declared ambient whose compiled argument is not the\\n  ambient literal refuses (compile-time AST verification); indirect-origin\\n  entries (`:dynamic` sites, the `:gate-site/none` entry site) refuse;\\n  variable context arguments are `/2`-only. A declared site id that never\\n  appears in any trace is a RECORDED DIAGNOSTIC\\n  (`:attribution :stale-site-diagnostics`), never silent non-credit. The\\n  `/3` self-delegation keeps its own unmapped site id: no credit, the\\n  originating call is the credited event.\\n- **H3-6 prep (the audit's query shape).** The independent audit\\n  re-derives the site tables from the same compiled ASTs, re-computes each\\n  fixture's canonical-source-hash, and re-runs the credit query over the\\n  two raw C-lane traces joined to the tables and the derived ambient\\n  correspondence; closure requires the reconstructed credit set to equal\\n  the gate's, with every withdrawn or gained witness explained.\\n\\nThe remainder of this document is the prior gate record, unchanged.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThe gate on the hardening line is **blocked**. The architect denied the prior\\n165/165 closure claim because membership in a static dependency closure did\\nnot prove execution of every arity. That claim is withdrawn. The gate retains\\nits final assertion `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))`; missing execution\\nevidence must fail that assertion.\\n\\nThe 106-fixture corpus has **100 passing agreements, two recorded deviations\\n(`elab-after-qed`, `check-after-qed`), two blocked fixtures, and two recorded\\nupstream failures.** The four narrowly recorded exception dispositions remain\\ndeclared departures, not agreements. No upstream or `src/cljc/` source changes\\nare made by H3-0. Admission is unchanged: 155 bindings (146 admitted, 9\\nexcluded) and 175 candidate function/arities (165 admitted, 10 excluded).\\n\\nRecorded executions establish **107/165** admitted arities: 39 directly\\nand 68 through named integrations. The other **58**, including `parse/1`,\\nremain uncredited. The declared departures are carried by the versioned\\n[`slice9_declarations.edn`](slice9_declarations.edn) (provenance `ea18c8e4^`),\\nrevalidated on every refresh by the representation-aware classifier: the\\nguest `:meta` value may be a pre-adoption raw closure or the admitted §8.10\\ndescriptor; structurally invalid descriptors and any payload, message, script\\nor call mismatch refuse (descriptor authenticity itself is the compiler's\\nadmission witness upstream of the outcome). The corrected counts and remaining arities\\nare recorded in [`slice9_evidence.edn`](slice9_evidence.edn) and\\n[`slice9_unexercised.edn`](slice9_unexercised.edn). The residual consumers in\\n[`fixture_closure.edn`](fixture_closure.edn) retain their concrete expected\\noutcomes; they do not establish closure of the full inventory, and their\\ncount (20) predates the re-derivation — the live unexercised set is the\\n58-name list.\\n\\n## Consumer evidence\\n\\n- `mkenv` preserves a nonempty global environment and creates empty locals.\\n- `beta-red`, `delta-normalize`, and `delta-normalize-local` have explicit\\n  entry fixtures and missing-reference rejections. The local wrapper also\\n  exercises explicit local definitions and their precedence over an ambient\\n  namespace definition.\\n- `install-unfold-implicit!` installs into both isolated upstream atoms on A.\\n  B/C return an updated immutable context, used by both the delta wrapper and\\n  NBE. Both normalizers read the same installed extension. An installed\\n  refusing extension propagates its original error data.\\n- `install-opacity-function` starts from a refusing policy, explicitly installs\\n  the working policy, then enters the original proof dispatcher through\\n  opaque/transparent steps and qed. A duplicate opaque step rejects. A uses\\n  an isolated namespace and host-local Var policy; B/C thread immutable\\n  definition updates through the explicit context.\\n- `install-fundamental-unparsers!` starts from an empty registry, installs the\\n  fundamental product unparser, then unparses nested implications. Dependent\\n  products and atoms remain unchanged. Direct `prod-impl-unparser` fixtures\\n  also verify its `[term false]` refusal result.\\n- `exists-kw?`, `term?`, `pair?`, and `vectorn?` include false results.\\n  `bound-vars` distinguishes a bound occurrence from entirely free variables.\\n  These fixtures preserve upstream behavior, including its shallow term\\n  validator and the use of `vector` rather than `vector?` in utility predicates.\\n- `proper-type?` enters each arity separately. Unknown variables throw;\\n  a well-typed term whose inferred type is not a sort returns false.\\n- `show-deftype` checks definition, axiom, theorem, implicit, and unknown\\n  labels. It depends only on portable record-kind predicates and returns a\\n  string. Host pprint and stdout functions remain excluded.\\n- `safe-get` covers successful lookup, missing keys, stored false, and stored\\n  nil. The latter three all reject upstream. `vremove` removes every match,\\n  preserves a no-match vector, and propagates a predicate's domain exception.\\n\\n`mkenv`, `appify`, and `bound-vars` have no domain rejection in the pinned\\nsource; the fixtures preserve their constructor, empty-input, and empty-set\\nresults instead of manufacturing refusals. A refused product rewrite is\\nidentified by its explicit modification flag, not mistaken for an exception.\\n\\nThe pinned local delta wrapper has a narrower portability scope than its\\ndocstring suggests: `delta-step` drops `local?` when calling `delta-reduction`\\non a reference. Consequently upstream can resolve a global or host namespace\\ndefinition on that path. The global-result fixture preserves this behavior;\\nthe namespace fixture supplies a local definition that shadows the ambient\\none. The guest boundary still requires explicit definitions and has no host\\nnamespace lookup capability. This round does not repair upstream or claim\\nagreement for ambient-only resolution.\\n\\n## Acceptance counting\\n\\nEvery selected guest function body appends `[guest-function arity]` to an\\nexplicit diagnostic stream at entry. Instrumentation covers all arities of\\nthe functions supplied to each fixture, including higher-order calls through\\nregistries and extension closures. Each C lane creates its own stream.\\nAfter the VM halts, the harness reads that stream through its own\\ncursor, preserving the fixture's original outcome and exception payload.\\nA/B remain uninstrumented. Raw ordered call records are retained under\\n`:c-walker :executed-calls` and `:c-semantic :executed-calls` for every completed\\nfixture. The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions per\\nlane. The instrumented fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound because\\nbody-entry stream writes add guest instructions. Reading the completed\\ndiagnostic stream is harness work after halt. This is an instrumentation\\nbudget change, not a new performance acceptance claim.\\n\\nPassing direct fixtures contribute only their original function/argument\\ncount, and only with matching body-entry records in both C lanes. Passing\\nnamed integrations contribute only exact arities recorded in both C lanes.\\nStatic dependency membership contributes no credit. Full branch coverage is\\nnot required. Context adapter identities and explicit extra context arguments\\nare recorded in the evidence; each observed guest arity is checked against\\nthat mapping individually, never against all arities of its function.\\n\\nOnly `:pass` fixture rows contribute exercise evidence. Recorded upstream\\nfailures and deviations do not contribute. Any admitted arity without a\\npassing direct or named integration execution path blocks the gate.\\n\\nThe accounting regression first failed against the old implementation: it\\ncredited the deliberately uncalled arity and accepted missing C-lane traces.\\nIt now requires both traces and leaves unused arities uncredited. A second\\nregression replaces the adapted `parse/1` body in memory with an unconditional\\nerror, then runs `:parse-to-normalize-to-type`. A/B and both C lanes still\\npass; both C traces record `parse/2` and no `parse/1`, and the counter leaves\\n`parse/1` uncredited. Every credited path is also checked against the recorded\\nexecutions of its named fixture. See\\n[`slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt`](slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt).\\n\\n## Recorded portability boundaries\\n\\nThe two `:recorded-deviation` rows remain `:elab-after-qed` and\\n`:check-after-qed`. Upstream embeds `clojure.core/meta`, a host function, in\\nexception data; C carries a guest closure. The original outcomes, comparison\\nflags, exact payload guards, and evidence pointers remain intact. Both rows\\nare listed in `:recorded-portability-boundaries` in the summary. Neither is\\nreported as agreement.\\n\\n## Recorded upstream failures\\n\\n`:typing-ascription` still reaches the upstream declaration\\n`type-of-ascribe`, which has no definition. A raises its original unbound-fn\\nexception; B/C retain the explicit branch-local refusal.\\n\\n`:compile-malformed` still passes scalar proof input `[42]`. A/B raise the\\noriginal native sequence exception; C retains its portable sequence refusal.\\n\\nThese two rows have the distinct disposition `:recorded-upstream-failure` and\\nare listed in `:recorded-upstream-failures`. Their original A/B/C records and\\nfalse agreement flags remain available. The disposition checks the exact\\nfixture ID, input call, exception class/message, B outcome, and both completed\\nC outcomes. Changed calls, IDs, or C payloads are tested to refuse the\\ndisposition. Any other execution failure remains a blocker. No upstream fix,\\naccepted-negative claim, or equality projection is introduced for these rows.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nAn independent audit re-derives the credited arities and fixture paths from\\nthe two raw C traces. Kondo reports zero errors and warnings. The full oracle\\nruns 26 tests and 1,697 assertions with exactly one failure and no errors:\\nits retained `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))` closure assertion. The\\nunexercised arities — **58** under the current accounting, including\\n`parse/1` — therefore continue to block acceptance. Verification results are\\nrecorded in [`slice9_verification.edn`](slice9_verification.edn), with command\\noutputs beside it.\\n`yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!` explicitly regenerates\\nboth execution evidence and the remaining-arity inventory; normal tests do\\nnot write them. Evidence retains the pinned upstream revision, compiler\\ndigest, runtime, instruction budget, per-fixture outcomes, diagnostic traces,\\ndependency graph, admission inventory, credited paths, and all four recorded\\nexception dispositions.\\n\\nThe append-only correction in [`known-gaps.md`](../../../docs/agents/known-gaps.md)\\nrecords that host Clojure turns a thrown string into `ClassCastException`,\\ncaught by `catch Exception` but not `catch ExceptionInfo`. Portable `try` binds\\nthe error payload without equivalent runtime class handling; this guest/host\\ngap remains declared.\\n\\nExecution scope is both C evaluators on the JVM. This correction does not\\nclaim renewed architect sign-off or Node/Dart verification, and the blocked\\ngate does not authorize program closure or merge.\\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-05 03:40:00 GMT (v1)\\nRevised-GMT: 2026-11-05 18:20:00 GMT (v2 — astra's four findings)\\nRevised-GMT: 2026-11-05 20:10:00 GMT (v3 — qwen3.8-max's five amendments)\\nRevised-GMT: 2026-11-06 02:45:00 GMT (v4 — kimi k3.1-pro's four amendments; verdict: endorse for owner sign-off with these)\\n# RULING OF RECORD — attribution-as-query: caller-side site tagging; record, then attribute by query\\n\\nStatus: SIGNED by the owner (2026-11-06, \\\"i sign-off\\\") after three independent reviews (gpt-6-astra v1: 4 findings; qwen3.8-max v2: 5 amendments; kimi k3.1-pro v3: 4 amendments — all incorporated). This document is now the ruling-of-record and the implementation contract.\\n\\nReview state: v1 → astra (4 findings); v2 → qwen3.8-max (5 amendments); v3 → kimi k3.1-pro (4 amendments, below). Architecture settled across all three; v4's changes are mechanical corrections to the mechanism and the battery, per kimi: \\\"(1) caller-side AST tagging; (2) case 5 redefined + a seventh case; (3) the trace-shape-induced revision of ALL pins and the accounting rewrite; (4) R1's trigger and format conditions.\\\" Central principle (all three accept): derive credit from recorded relationships, require actual body entry in both lanes, refuse ambiguity. Unitarity preserves what flows through the pipeline; it cannot recover provenance never recorded — this ruling records the missing provenance minimally, then attributes by query.\\n\\n## R1 — The durable correspondence record is DESCOPED, on stated conditions\\n\\nAs v3: the address-linked adaptation manifest is deferred — the adapter is inlined per fixture, addresses need canonicalization nothing yet consumes, and no second consumer exists. TWO CONDITIONS from kimi's review: (a) **the deferred trigger is an OWNER/ARCHITECT call** — \\\"a second consumer exists\\\" is never self-declared by an implementer; (b) **the declared site tables are recorded in a stable, versioned evidence format** so the later R1 landing is an addition to the record, not a migration of it. The long-term stream-citizen direction stands as design intent. The offset table `kernel-context-extra-arguments` is retired — BUT its retirement has mechanical scope (see R6): it serves the context-API arities across the whole family, and its consumers (kernel-executed-arity? and ~30 pinned assertions) are rewritten with it.\\n\\n## R2 — The mechanism: CALLER-SIDE site tagging in the compiled AST; the callee record carries the caller's site id\\n\\n**Site ids are assigned at APPLICATION EXPRESSIONS in the compiled AST, post-macroexpansion** — not at callee body entry, and not on raw source forms (the corpus runs under `is`/`testing`/LaTTe macros; source-level tagging would silently miss every macro-expanded call site). The callee-entry trace record is extended to carry the **caller's site id**: the record becomes `[fname arity caller-site-id]`. Rationale (kimi's finding): the ambiguity is one guest callee clause serving two upstream arities — callee-side extension yields identical records for both origins and cannot work. Consequence for the scoping inventory: the **walker/semantic ingress row is updated** — the walker gains site-id stamping at application nodes; it is not \\\"nothing further.\\\" Indirect applications (`(:implicit-fn implicit-def)` and kin) have static expression positions, so they receive static site ids like any other call; the callee being runtime-unknown does not affect the id. Recursion is safe (existence-based consumers). The `/3` self-delegation gets its own unmapped site id → no credit — the originating-call rule (R3) is expressible only under this caller-side form, which is why the ruling mandates it.\\n\\n## R3 — Disjoint attribution patterns, verified by caller-site linkage\\n\\nA body entry attributes to upstream `/1` only via a site whose compiled argument expression is the ambient literal (`empty-env` supplied by the adapter's declared path); explicit-context sites attribute to `/2`. Disjointness is by recorded site identity and compiled argument shape, never by value equality.\\n\\n## R2b — The refusal battery: SEVEN cases\\n\\n1. An explicit `/2` call supplying an empty environment must NOT credit `/1`.\\n2. An unexecuted ambient `/1` beside an executed explicit `/2`: no borrowing.\\n3. Mismatched program/adaptation evidence: attribution refuses. **The referent is defined**: the mismatch is the canonical-source-hash of the inlined adapter, computed by the compiler during instrumentation and recorded per fixture — a trace from a fixture whose recorded hash differs refuses.\\n4. Missing-lane evidence: attribution refuses.\\n5. **REDEFINED** (kimi: the v3 case was unimplementable — the tagged trace records no arguments): the fixture's declared call shape is verified against the **compiled AST argument expression at that site** — a site declared ambient whose AST argument is not the ambient literal refuses. The check is compile-time, not value-sniffing.\\n6. Indirect-origin: body entries originating through indirect application refuse unless site-linked; default refusal (static ids make indirect sites linkable — they are not exempt).\\n7. **NEW (kimi)**: variable/derived argument shapes — a site whose context argument is a variable (bound to `empty-env` on one path, a populated env on another) is statically unclassifiable: **default refusal or `/2`-only attribution**; the declaration is checked against the AST argument expression (an `empty-env` literal may claim ambient; anything else may not).\\n8. **NEW (kimi, diagnostic)**: a declared site whose id never appears in any trace (stale table after a fixture edit) is a RECORDED DIAGNOSTIC — a mistyped table must not masquerade as honest refusal.\\n\\nThe `/3` self-delegation: the delegating call gets its own unmapped site id → no credit; the originating call is the credited event.\\n\\n## R4 — The attribution contract is versioned where the rule lives\\n\\nUnchanged from v3: the differential gate record (slice9_gate.md) versions the attribution section; `yin.cic.spec` v1 is untouched; \\\"mapped\\\" is defined by the declared site tables + caller-site-tagged records; name+arity matching is the degenerate 1:1 optimization.\\n\\n## R5 — Closure is MEASURED; the revision scope is HONEST about its blast radius\\n\\nThe attribution may expose unsupported credit among previously credited arities; valid witnesses preserved, withdrawn witnesses reported, H3-6 blocked until independent reconstruction succeeds. **The revision scope (kimi's correction of v3's under-statement): the trace shape change (2-vector → 3-vector) touches EVERY pin and path set built as 2-vector literals** — the refusal pins (`contains?` assertions on `[registered-definition? 2]`), every `kernel-executed-arity?` path set across the 20-arity family's ~30 assertions, and the gate-status computation (which must learn the third field or the credit set misparses). All of it is authorized by this ruling and listed in the evidence. \\\"No valid pin regresses\\\" means: pins encoding current semantics do not *silently* regress; pins requiring mechanical shape updates are updated and listed; pins encoding superseded semantics are revised on the record.\\n\\n## R6 — The retirement of the offset table is SCOPED to its real consumers\\n\\n`kernel-context-extra-arguments` serves the context-API arities across the family (not just F2) and is consumed by `kernel-executed-arity?`. Retiring it means **rewriting the accounting predicate** — the declared site tables must cover every context-API arity it served, or the retirement is partial and two mechanisms coexist (the failure qwen's amendment 4 warned against). The implementation round states the coverage list explicitly before deleting the table. The refusal pins' shape updates are covered by R5's authorization. (v3's \\\"the refusal pins are untouched\\\" is corrected: they are *mechanically updated* to the 3-vector shape, on the record.)\\n\\n## R7 — H3-6's audit runs the query — and re-derives the site tables\\n\\nUnchanged from v3, plus kimi's trust-model hardening: **the declared site tables are DERIVED MECHANICALLY from the compiled AST during instrumentation** (the compiler sees each site's argument expression), and H3-6's independent audit **re-derives them** from the same record — a wrong declaration is a compile/audit failure, not an honor-system risk.\\n\\n## Scoping inventory (astra + qwen + kimi reviewed)\\n\\n| Layer | Present now | Missing for the query |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Source/adaptation | pinned upstream source, `context.edn`, host assembly + rewrites | declared site tables (mechanically derived; versioned format); retired offset table |\\n| Compilation | `kernel-compile` AST per fixture (adapter INLINED; canonical source hash computed) | CALLER-SIDE site-id stamping at application nodes (post-expansion); per-fixture hash recording |\\n| Walker/semantic ingress | AST → datoms appended to a program medium | **UPDATED**: application-node site-id stamping in the walker; callee records extended with the caller's site id |\\n| Execution evidence | ordered body-entry pairs, both C lanes, outcomes | the third trace field (caller site id); the declared site tables |\\n| Trace/budget | `stream/make` 1000000; 2M-bound precedent | restated capacity + instruction bound for the added field |\\n| Gate accounting | manifest-derived denominator, name/arity matching; 2-vector trace literals throughout | `dao.space.query/q` attribution + the site tables + the 3-vector migration |\\n| Manifest schema | schema-1, CLOSED key set | nothing (linkage evidence is out-of-band; schema-2 only if R1's durable record later lands) |\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- The SEVEN-case battery + the stale-table diagnostic: all refusals refuse; the disjoint patterns attribute correctly on both lanes.\\n- The attribution reconstructs the credit set; withdrawn witnesses reported; 165/165 only if every attribution is supported.\\n- The pin revisions (mechanical shape updates + the semantic /1 re-credit) listed in the evidence; the `:gate-status` assertion PASSES for the first time; H3-6's independent audit re-derives the site tables and completes closure with final architect sign-off.\\n- No valid pin silently regresses; prior rulings stand; the trace capacity restated before any tagged-trace run; R1's deferred trigger reserved to the owner/architect.\\n\\n## Implementation ordering\\n\\nFirst deliverable: the written inventory confirmation (the instrumentation touch points, the capacity measurement, the offset-table coverage list). Then: caller-side site-id stamping in the walker/compile → the mechanically derived site tables → the seven-case battery + diagnostic → the accounting rewrite + pin migration → the attribution + re-credit → H3-6.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793953025937-reviewer-h3-6-audit.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:16:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md; cat test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md; cat deps.edn'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-11-05 03:40:00 GMT (v1)\\nRevised-GMT: 2026-11-05 18:20:00 GMT (v2 — astra's four findings)\\nRevised-GMT: 2026-11-05 20:10:00 GMT (v3 — qwen3.8-max's five amendments)\\nRevised-GMT: 2026-11-06 02:45:00 GMT (v4 — kimi k3.1-pro's four amendments; verdict: endorse for owner sign-off with these)\\n# RULING OF RECORD — attribution-as-query: caller-side site tagging; record, then attribute by query\\n\\nStatus: SIGNED by the owner (2026-11-06, \\\"i sign-off\\\") after three independent reviews (gpt-6-astra v1: 4 findings; qwen3.8-max v2: 5 amendments; kimi k3.1-pro v3: 4 amendments — all incorporated). This docume